cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its trained models in your work, please cite it as follows."
title: "MedKnow: Teaching Medical AI When Not to Know"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Open-source benchmark for uncertainty-aware referral and selective prediction
  in chest X-ray classification. ResNet-18 trained on Kermany chest X-rays with
  patient-level splitting; MC Dropout, MSP, and entropy uncertainty estimation;
  referral/selective-prediction analysis with random controls; temperature
  scaling; and external validation on RSNA and NIH ChestXray-14 showing that
  uncertainty-guided referral works in-domain but fails under domain shift.
authors:
  - name: "<Corresponding author name>"
  - name: "<Additional author>"
date-released: "2026-08-14"
keywords:
  - medical-ai
  - chest radiograph
  - uncertainty quantification
  - selective prediction
  - referral
  - calibration
  - external validation
  - domain shift
license: MIT
